---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageIntro from "../components/PageIntro.astro";
import { PROGRAM_URL, VERIFIED_ON } from "../data/portal";
---
<Base title="About & Methodology">
  <PageIntro title="About & Methodology" eyebrow="A traceable, carefully scoped record" description="How this portal connects workshop context, scientific questions and possible research actions while preserving uncertainty." />
  <section><h2>Purpose &amp; scope</h2><p>This independent local prototype is intended for participants of the 2nd Workshop on Organisation and Maintenance of Tropical Convection and the Madden Julian Oscillation, held at ICTP in Trieste, 26–30 October 2026.</p><p>Its interface supports chronological browsing and topic-based exploration. It does not represent an official ICTP publication or an agreed scientific record.</p></section>
  <section><h2>What has been verified</h2><dl class="method-list"><dt>Program metadata</dt><dd>The five-day schedule is based on the <a href={PROGRAM_URL} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">official ICTP timetable</a>, checked {VERIFIED_ON}. The timetable's overlapping session blocks are preserved and explained. Within academic blocks, individual talk start times are shown; breaks are noted.</dd><dt>Sample video</dt><dd><a href="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RPXnSvabsGY" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RPXnSvabsGY</a> is a 1:00 unlisted highlight. Its YouTube title and description match the Themes 3 + 4 breakout listed for 27 October, 16:30–18:00 Europe/Rome. It is not the following day's plenary report.</dd><dt>Scientific coverage</dt><dd>No reviewed scientific summaries, positions, findings or question classifications have been imported. The question and action detail pages are explicitly labeled interface placeholders. Unavailable content is not reconstructed.</dd><dt>Publication permissions</dt><dd>Local demonstration of the supplied sample was requested. Public website publication permissions and final representative-version approval remain pending. Unlisted visibility alone does not establish publication permission.</dd></dl></section>
  <section><h2>Editorial method</h2><dl class="method-list"><dt>Evidence before interpretation</dt><dd>Future summaries must use reviewed meeting minutes and explicitly approved publication derivatives. Observations, interpretations, hypotheses, proposals and documented agreements will remain distinct.</dd><dt>Provenance and review</dt><dd>Approved records will preserve source identifiers, versions, review status, record coverage and uncertainty. Source changes require reassessment. CMS publication controls alone do not establish scientific review.</dd><dt>Attribution</dt><dd>Named speakers appear only for individual talks in the official program. Discussion sessions are not assigned individual names or inferred positions.</dd><dt>Agreement and coverage</dt><dd>Emerging alignment is not formal consensus. Silence does not demonstrate agreement. A short highlight cannot establish complete coverage of a session.</dd><dt>Research actions</dt><dd>Action pages show possible AI agent workflows, not assigned responsibilities, deadlines, commitments or completed work. The current example is generic editorial copy awaiting scientific grounding.</dd></dl></section>
  <section><h2>Media &amp; access</h2><p>Videos remain on YouTube and load only when requested by the viewer. No video files, original slides, PDFs, Word files, raw transcripts, rapporteur notes or original photographs are hosted or offered for download.</p><p>The interface uses English throughout, visible keyboard focus, a skip link, responsive layouts and player controls. Captions and accessibility of the source video depend on the available YouTube track; no reviewed transcript is available here.</p><p>The site runs locally on loopback. Public deployment requires separate authorization.</p></section>
</Base>
